                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 13 at 11:35AM MST until September 13 at 1:30PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "At 1135 AM MST, Doppler radar indicated that heavy rain has moved\neast of the Havasupai Creek drainage north of Supai, though\nadditional storms are possible through the afternoon. Between 0.5 and\n1 inch of rain fell earlier this morning. Flash flooding is ongoing\nor expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nnormally dry washes.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nBeaver Falls, Mooney Falls and Little Navajo Falls.\n\nThis includes the Colorado River between river miles 156 and 158.\n\nThis includes the following recreation areas and campgrounds...\nSecond Chance Camp Site.\n\nThis includes the following swimming holes...\nAll swimming holes on Havasu Creek near Supai.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nSinyella Canyon, Colorado River, Little Coyote Canyon and Havasu\nCreek.",
                "instruction": "Flooding of washes and creeks will occur, including Havasupai Creek.\n\nGet out of washes and creeks if you are camping or hiking! Flooding\nis occurring or imminent and will inundate creeks and washes.",
                "response": "Avoid",
